From e9bc3cf8e71fa0269d3ec56cfce1abb73509851a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missing goal video links when the clip title has no
 opponent

Some goal clips have non-standard titles (e.g. "REG26-Evander-Goal"), so
the scoring side falls back to the slug. The slug names the opponent by
full name ("goal-e-da-silva-ferreira-vs-d-c-united-35"), which never
equalled the three-letter code ("DC"), and unrecognised opponents
defaulted to the home side, so away goals lost their link.

- Match the opponent from the title or slug against each team's code,
  full name and short name (accent/punctuation-insensitive)
- Strip the full minute ("-45-3") and "-x1234" dedupe suffix from slugs
- Leave the side unknown instead of assuming home; such clips match a
  goal by minute only, after same-side clips
- Move parsing/matching to src/goal-videos.ts with node:test tests,
  type-checked via tsconfig.test.json, and run them in the scheduled
  workflow

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
